{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:08:53.768Z","data":{"text":"Implemented task 1.\n\n**Summary**\n- Added first-attempt pre-spawn verify to the Rust run feature: it runs after approval, before the scope snapshot and pi, using the same verify path/env/timeout as the run verdict.\n- Added pre-spawn `verify_ran` fields (`phase`, `expected`, `mismatch`, `missingPaths`), log writing, and the `verify_precondition` dead marker.\n- Copied the named-path tokenizer and missing-path rules into `feature/named.rs`, resolving globs through rust-loop `scope_files`.\n- Added `tests/run_pre_spawn.rs` covering all four new scenarios, plus named-path edge cases.\n- Updated existing run tests for the task verify's new `1-2.log` numbering and the `1-9.log/keep` collision folder.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify passed.\n- `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` with `OSQ_CHANGE` passed.\n- cargo-mutants over every changed source file reported no missed mutants.\n\n**Result**\nWritten to `openspec/changes/311-rust-run-baseline-verify/.run/results/1.md`.\n\nOne deviation is documented there: the delta table lists `missingPaths` as none for the `test -f src/a.txt` rows, but the requirement text and TypeScript rules make `src/a.txt` a missing path in that fixture. The tests assert the requirement-derived value."}}
